// Derivative-propagation probe (see docs/OSL-INTEGRATION.md, "Feed OSL the surface derivatives").
// Outputs the world-space filter footprint of P, which is zero unless the renderer supplies the
// sample derivatives sg.dPdx/dPdy. The [.deriv] test uses it to prove those derivatives reach the
// shader -- the prerequisite for filterwidth()/texture()/antialiasing.
shader deriv_probe(output float Disp = 0.0)
{
    Disp = length(filterwidth(P));
}
